    "lawCode": "Add §3615, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2657\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to establishing the\nbilingual teachers of tomorrow teacher recruitment and retention program\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo set forth requirements and guidelines for the Bilingual Teachers of\nTomorrow Recruitment and Retention Program.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Adds a new section to Education Law to establish the bilin-\ngual teachers of tomorrow recruitment and retention program.  This\nsection details the application, grants, and funding allocation for the\nprogram.\n\nSection 2. Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will enfranchise a segment of the population that would bene-\nfit from this type of funding.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-22: S.5433-Passed Senate\n\n2019-20: S.5027-Referred to Education\n\n2017-18: S.2700-Referred to Education\n\n2015-16: S.2867-Referred to Education\n\n2013-14: S.3093-Referred to Education\n\n2011-12: S.1160-Referred to Education\n\n2009-10: S.2543/A.4461 - Referred to Education\n\n2007-08: S.2713/A.-4872\n\n2005-06: A.4384\n\n2003-04: A.5309\n\n2001-02: A.5986\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
